{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Fastest Man Alive" is the second episode of The CW series "The Flash".","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The episode was written by Andrew Kreisberg and Geoff Johns from a story by Greg Berlanti and Kreisberg and directed by David Nutter.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was first broadcast on October 14, 2014 in The CW.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The show is itself an spin-off of the show "Arrow", where many characters in the series were introduced during the second season.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The episode revolves about Barry Allen (Grant Gustin), a CSI forensic scientist working for the Central City Police Department.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" During a visit to an event, the event is robbed by masked men.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" This is later revealed as the result of an accident during the accelerator explosion and the men are in fact a man who can duplicate himself.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The episode also shows flashbacks when Barry tries to see his dad in jail, to Joe's disapproval.","title":"Fastest Man Alive"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""The Flash" is an American television series developed by writer-producers Greg Berlanti, Andrew Kreisberg and Geoff Johns, based on the DC Comics character the Flash.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The series premiered in the United States on October 7, 2014, on The CW television network.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is a spin-off from "Arrow", a show in the same universe.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The first season follows police forensic investigator Barry Allen (Grant Gustin), who develops super-speed after he is struck by lightning.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" In his attempt to learn about his powers and how to use them for good, he is assisted by S.T.A.R. Labs' Dr. Caitlin Snow (Danielle Panabaker), Cisco Ramon (Carlos Valdes) and Dr. Harrison Wells (Tom Cavanagh).","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" Barry also tries to solve the murder of his mother (Michelle Harrison) by a superhuman attacker (Matt Letscher) when he was eleven.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The murder investigation unjustly imprisoned his father (John Wesley Shipp), leaving detective Joe West (Jesse L. Martin), father of his best friend, Iris (Candice Patton), to take in the young Barry.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The memory of his mother's murder and his father's framing and later killing motivates Barry to put his personal needs aside and use his powers to fight those who would hurt the innocent, shaping him into the Flash.","title":"List of The Flash characters"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Greg Douglas is a fictional character from the BBC medical drama "Holby City", played by actor Edward MacLiam.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He first appeared in the series ten episode "Together Alone", broadcast on 17 February 2010.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Greg was introduced as a new Cardiothoracic surgical registrar working at the hospital's Darwin ward.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Producers created an affiliation with long-standing character Connie Beauchamp (Amanda Mealing) and played a short romance.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Greg is characterised as an ambitious, abrasive, rebellious medical professional.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" He has "Irish charm" and will often use it to his advantage.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Greg's fictional backstory detailed him growing up in Dublin, Ireland.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" MacLiam has said producers wanted a "North Side Dubliner" with a more aggressive persona than other characters to feature in the series.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" One of the character's initial stories featured him mentoring F2 junior doctor Oliver Valentine (James Anderson).","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" The show developed a "bromance" between the two and they were depicted either arguing or joking their way through scenes.","title":"Greg Douglas (Holby City)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Greg Berlanti (born May 24, 1972) is an American film and television writer and producer.","title":"Greg Berlanti"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is known for his work on the television series "Dawson's Creek", "Everwood", "Political Animals"; and for his contributions to DC Comics on film and television, including The CW's "Arrowverse".","title":"Greg Berlanti"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2017 Berlanti set the record in having 10 different scripted television series planned to air in the 2017–18 television season on various networks and digital platforms.","title":"Greg Berlanti"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""Pilot" is the first episode of The CW series "The Flash".","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The episode was written by Andrew Kreisberg and Geoff Johns, based on a story by Greg Berlanti, Kreisberg, and Johns, and directed by David Nutter.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was first broadcast on October 7, 2014, on The CW.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The show is a spin-off from "Arrow" where many of the characters in "The Flash" were introduced during its second season.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The episode revolves around Barry Allen (Grant Gustin), a forensic scientist working for the Central City Police Department.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" On the night of the launch of a particle accelerator, a malfunction causes it to explode during a storm.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" At the same time, Barry is struck by lightning.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" He wakes from a coma after nine months, and discovers that he has developed a new power: super speed.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" He is helped by S.T.A.R. Labs' personnel, led by Dr. Harrison Wells (Tom Cavanagh), who are trying to control his speed so that he can use it for greater good.","title":"Pilot (The Flash)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""The Flash" is an American action television series developed by Greg Berlanti, Andrew Kreisberg, and Geoff Johns, airing on The CW.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is based on the DC Comics character Barry Allen / Flash, a costumed crimefighter with the power to move at superhuman speeds.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is a spin-off from "Arrow", existing in the same fictional universe.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The series follows Barry Allen, portrayed by Grant Gustin, a crime scene investigator who gains superhuman speed, which he uses to fight criminals, including others who have also gained superhuman abilities.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "The Flash" was renewed in March 2016 for a third season, which premiered on October 4, 2016.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" On January 8, 2017, The CW renewed the series for a fourth season, which is scheduled to debut on October 10, 2017.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" s of 23, 2017, episodes of "The Flash " have aired, concluding the first half of the  season.","title":"List of The Flash episodes"}],"peer_messages":["0,"text":"\"The Flash\" is an American television series developed by writer-producers Greg Berlanti, Andrew Kreisberg and Geoff Johns, based on the DC Comics character the Flash.","title":"List of The Flash characters"}
